==Trivia==
*Puffsley's Comet's name is a portmanteau of ''pufferfish'' and ''[[wikipedia:Halley's Comet|Halley's Comet]]''.
*Puffsley's Comet's Japanese name (超新星テッサー, ''Chōshinsei Tessā'', "Supernova Tessar" or "Supernova Tesser") may contain a pun on てっさ ''tessa'' (a [[wikipedia:Kansai dialect|Kansai]] term for fugu sashimi) and クエーサー ''kuēsā'' (quasar).
*According to his Japanese description, Puffsley's Comet fits best with the sin of greed among the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]].
*The line, "Rolls at high speeds in pursuit of shiny things," (輝くものを追って高速で転がる) in his Japanese description uses part of a lyric from the song "[[wikipedia:Earthly Stars (Unsung Heroes)|Earthly Stars (Unsung Heroes)]]" by [[wikipedia:Miyuki Nakajima|Miyuki Nakajima]]. The lyric in question is "Kagayaku mono o otte" (輝くものを追って), literally meaning "Pursue shiny things".
*Puffsley's Comet and his debut stage's reward, [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Mightycat]], both have high speed, many knockbacks, extremely short foreswing and full backswing. Furthermore, both of them can grow larger (Puffsley's Comet in his attack animation, Mightycat in his Evolved Form), and Puffsley's Comet is an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] like Mightycat's inspiration, [[wikipedia:Superman|Superman]], while Mightycat's Evolved Form is an aspiring singer like Puffsley's Comet.

